# Task 033 (RFC-019 §7, Review 194): line-ending checkout is otherwise left
# to each Git client's own `core.autocrlf` default -- `true` on Git for
# Windows, the tool `windows-latest` CI runners use. With no override here,
# text files checked out on Windows arrive with CRLF, which broke a strict,
# LF-anchored `include_str!` split in orbok-models (Task 032's finding).
#
# Repo-wide, not scoped to the seven files that happen to be exposed today
# (six SQL migrations, one RFC appendix): the failure mode of a narrower
# pattern is *silence* -- a CRLF file that still happens to parse -- and
# scoping it correctly requires remembering to extend the pattern every time
# a new `include_str!` of a text file is added. No binary files are tracked
# in this repository (confirmed at the time this was written), so `text=auto`
# has nothing to misclassify.
* text=auto eol=lf
